From e087b0037ccbd29d50bb0dad8894bc987fe6ffd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:26:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0225: Replayable Quest Chains -- the loot mechanism itself

Step (2) of the sequencing plan. Loot math only, no UI, no engine
action, no way to actually trigger a replay yet.

Padding loot: two new LootSourceTag values ('chainReplayHeroic'/
'chainReplayLegendary'), own budget multipliers (1.3x/1.8x, distinct
from raid's 1.5x/2.2x -- chain replay is lighter-weight, not a second
raid ladder) and own display labels ([Replay: Heroic]/[Replay:
Legendary], distinct from raid's bare [Heroic]/[Legendary]).

Dedicated item: new scaleChainExclusiveItem() in proceduralLoot.ts --
a genuinely different mechanism from the padding case, since
chainExclusive rewards are permanently exempt from procedural
generation (never isProceduralTemplate()). Multiplies the item's own
authored mods/stats directly. 1.3x/1.7x multipliers verified
numerically against gravewatchers_band's real pre-0214 tiered values
-- exact match (success 6->8->10, injuryResist 14->18->24).

Caught and handled a real asymmetry: HeroManager.equipmentMods does
customMods ?? def.mods (full replacement) while equipmentStats does
def.stats + enchantStats (additive). scaleChainExclusiveItem returns
customMods as the full scaled total but enchantStatsDelta as only the
difference above base, matching each field's actual combination rule.

EquipmentManager.instantiate gained a second branch for chainExclusive
+ the two new tags. Deliberately doesn't set rolledItemLevel -- gear
relevance decay falls back to def.reqLevel, same as every other
authored item.

4 new Tuning entries. No new equipment.json content -- confirmed, not
needed for this step.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean. Scaling
math checked numerically against real precedent, not just read for
plausibility.
